AB  - For safer and more repeatable penetration testing, we introduce AgentPentestAI, a multi-agent framework that makes use of large language models (LLMs). The system balances cost, information gain, and success probability by integrating an Orchestrator, Recon, Knowledge, Exploit, Memory, and Validator agent with utility-based scheduling (θ, ξ, η). Assessments on 20 HackTheBox/VulnHub targets reveal that 68 percent of subtasks are completed, compared to 52 percent for PentestGPT, and that hallucinations have decreased from 12 percent to 5 percent. Rollback validation, disallow lists, and sandboxing are used to enforce safety. The findings demonstrate how AgentPentestAI may increase automation dependability while meeting security standards for the healthcare industry.
