AB  - Industrial environments increasingly integrate operational technology (OT) with information technology (IT), expanding the cyber-attack surface and generating large volumes of heterogeneous security alerts. This complexity makes it difficult for analysts to triage and investigate threats across IT systems, Industrial IoT devices, and OT networks (e.g., industrial control system logs, protocol-level events such as Modbus traffic, and Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) alerts). In this paper, we present CoAnalyst, an “intelligent cybersecurity analyst” that acts as a security copilot to support human analysts. CoAnalyst is an agentic, OT-oriented framework that can be deployed at the edge on resource-constrained hardware while performing OT protocol-level alert correlation, enabling it to fuse and interpret alerts from multiple data sources close to where they are generated. It automates routine investigation steps and provides structured, easy-to-read contextual information. Its chat interface and agentic architecture enable dynamic toolcalling based on user intent, allowing adaptive investigation of OT networks, contextual reasoning over retrieved data, and ondemand threat analysis.
ER  - 

