AB  - With the rapid increase of advanced persistent threats in critical information infrastructure, it’s vital to evaluate the security level and spot the possible vulnerabilities ahead to avoid severe consequences of cyber-attacks. However, the complexity of APT made it difficult to simulate real life red teaming. In this paper, we present DeepAttacker, an end-to-end cooperative multi-agent collaboration based red teaming system featuring life-cycle attacking simulation. By employing multi-agent collaboration, the attack simulation process can be more intelligent, covering more attack actions and finalizing efficient attack chains, helps uncover deeply concealed vulnerabilities. Comprehensive experiments indicated DeepAttacker has a broader attack action space and higher rate of exploitation rate compared with other frameworks, achieved 5 x attack action coverage, which makes it suitable for application in simulating real-life APT attacks and spotting deeply concealed vulnerabilities.
