AB  - The current global robotics market is oriented towards more intensive integration of robots into human-centric environments. Service, medical, and humanoid robots are becoming more widely used thanks to their interconnectedness through IoT, and humans are more reliant on their autonomous behaviors than ever. Even though these benefits improve people's lives, cybersecurity issues become a major concern. Therefore, in this paper, we propose an algorithm for detecting cyber-attacks on the mobile robot perception system. Two types of cyber-attacks are formulated as false-data injection attacks on the mobile robot's vision system. The foundation model NVLabs C-RADIOv4 is used as a feature extractor to generate general-purpose visual features, which are fed to a Mahalanobis distance output head to determine whether a cyber-attack has targeted a sequence of RGB images. The proposed algorithm is tested on the PAL TIAGo mobile robot with ROS.
