AB  - The Internet of Things (IoT) has provided real-time connectivity across smart environments but has also been vulnerable to cyberattacks. We propose IoT-CyberAgent, a novel real-time multi-agent IoT threat mitigation and recommendation system that integrates large language models (LLMs) with machine learning techniques. IoT-CyberAgent performs real-time feature engineering to classify specific IoT attacks, and the recommendation agent provides mitigation strategies through contextual searches. Experimental results demonstrate improved detection accuracy, real-time adaptability, and effective recommendation solutions. This system addresses the need for better attack detection and response in IoT environments by combining classical ML models and LLMs for deeper understanding and contextual recommendations.
