AB  - Cyber-Physical Systems (CPS) are systems that combine computer, communication and physical operations that are essential in the infrastructure of the present day. Nevertheless, the galloping growth of CPS in areas like smart grids, transport, healthcare, and industrial IoT has also predisposed them to complex cyberattacks. Conventional AI-based security designs are computationally limited in nature and lack fine-tuning detection in the face of zero-day attacks, adversarial samples, or high-dimensional CPS data. This review introduces a Quantum Generative AI Hybrid Framework that would be used to advance the security of CPS with the help of quantum feature encoding, quantum generative adversarial networks (QGANs), and hybrid classical-quantum fusion models. The comparative analysis shows that QGAI has better qualities compared to classical models in terms of the quality of detecting anomalies, predicting, and robustness of the system. The paper also pinpoints the difficulties, open research questions and future avenues on the integration of QGAI within real world CPS security developments.
ER  - 

