AB  - Dark web is a critical but long-overlooked source of Cyber Threat Intelligence (CTI), where various actors usually engage in illegal activities, such as malware dissemination, zero-day exploit trade, and credential compromises. However, the high volume and unstructured nature of dark web data pose formidable challenges in efficient and substantial threat discovery and assessment. This work proposes a web scraping-based, automated Dark Web Intelligence System with Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Large Language Models (LLMs) to obtain actionable CTI. The system relies on Beautiful Soup(BS4) for spidering of .onion sites, Sentence Transformers for semantic threat typing, and a high-accuracy DistilBERT model. Threat metadata is enriched with severity scores, probable impact, and suggested mitigation steps, and stored in a centralized database for retrieval through a secure admin interface. A real-time automated dashboard provides URL scanning, interactive reporting, and trend analysis, with threat reporting sent at regular intervals. Empirical testing of the system shows a 72% accuracy level in threat prediction, which reflects the efficiency of the system in real-time extraction of CTI. The method provides a viable and intelligent solution to proactive cybersecurity defines against oncoming threats from the dark web.
ER  - 

