AB  - As cyber threats grow in complexity, blue team defenders require robust systems for multi-stage analysis. We introduce ThreatSage, a modular benchmark for evaluating Large Language Models (LLMs) in orchestrated blue team defense operations. ThreatSage defines a structured function-calling pipeline across four stages: threat attribution, behavioral analysis, prioritization, and mitigation. Each stage integrates domain-specific functions such as entity extraction and response generation. The benchmark comprises 30 task types and over 450,000 instances sourced from 23 threat intelligence datasets. Experiments across leading LLMs show that ThreatSage improves precision, task dependency handling, and robustness against noise, outperforming prompting-based methods like Chain-of-Thought. ThreatSage establishes a realistic framework for secure, autonomous threat reasoning in operational environments.
ER  - 

