AB  - Cloud environments get much more complex, the traditional security model is no longer equipped to handle such attacks. ZTA or zero trust architecture is often referred to as a security model for the mind, assuming that any and every system cannot be trusted. However, traditional ZTA implementations tend to be rather stable. This study proposes a framework that can develop a self-directed automated cloud security system through Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA), using Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) and Reinforcement Learning (RL). The system automatically responds to attacks by observing the behavior of the sub-systems. After observing it response, it can update and modify the attack policy in a real time. With GenAI to formulate the policies, and Reinforcement Learning (RL) for decision making through feedback, this system strengthens security posture, improves threat detection and enforces Zero Trust compliance. The system can respond to new threats and vulnerabilities. This makes the cloud infrastructures more resilient. The first assessment revealed that the proposed system is better than existing models in terms of flexibility, efficiency, and protection against cyber threats.
