AB  - The digitization of cultural heritage, while expanding its accessibility and scientific value, increases its vulnerability to increasingly sophisticated cyber threats, with potential impacts on preservation, integrity and public trust. Cultural institutions, similar in size and operations to Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs), face increasing cybersecurity challenges, hampered by limited resources, lack of expertise, and regulatory complexities. This article presents PACY (Pro-Active Cybersecurity), an innovative Artificial Intelligence-based platform designed to simplify cybersecurity management for such entities. PACY leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) through a specialized multi-agent architecture, in which dedicated AI agents, refined through prompt engineering, guide non-expert users through diagnosis and incident response. By natively integrating Open Source Intelligence (OSINT) sources such as VirusTotal and IntelX, and offering natural language interaction, PACY simplifies threat analysis. A distinguishing feature is the automatic generation of structured incident reports, essential for compliance and escalation. Initial validation shows how PACY significantly reduces cognitive load and improves operational effectiveness compared to generalist LLMs, bridging the skills gap for cultural institutions.
