AB  - Low-altitude remote sensing network technology has advanced rapidly, especially with the assistance of large language models (LLMs). The use of LLMs, especially with unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) in remote sensing systems, poses significant security and privacy risks due to the need to transmit sensitive information and to enable large-scale distributed communication. This paper introduces the Quantum AI Security Framework (QL Sec) for LLM-powered low-altitude remote sensing networks. The proposed solution utilizes a hybrid Quantum AI security mechanism designed to enhance confidentiality, integrity, and authentication, and to resist adversarial intrusions. The framework also uses quantum-secured encryption and privacy-preserving feature perturbation to help reduce information leakage during edge-cloud communication. Results reveal that the proposed framework achieves 96.41% attack detection accuracy, a secret key rate (SKR) of 0.91 bits/use, and a reduced quantum bit error rate (QBER) of 0.029. SHAP explainability analysis validates the contribution of quantum-secure and quantum-safe components to trustworthy decision-making. The proposed Quantum AI-based system provides an efficient, scalable, and highly secure solution for future intelligent low-altitude remote sensing systems.
ER  - 

