AB  - Facing the core challenges of traditional code vulnerability repair, which heavily relies on expert experience, is inefficient, and difficult to scale, this paper explores a new automated repair approach based on generative artificial intelligence. The study aims to build an intelligent repair mechanism that integrates deep semantic understanding with code generation capabilities. The core of this mechanism lies in leveraging large language models to perform joint reasoning on code context and vulnerability patterns, thereby automatically synthesizing repair patches that maintain semantic consistency and functional correctness. This paper details how to embed the AIGC repair engine into an automated ‘detection-repair-verification’ loop and introduces the key technologies used to improve repair accuracy, guided by a retrieval-enhanced knowledge base of vulnerabilities. Through practical validation in the ‘ZhiHu’ system, this mechanism provides a feasible technical solution and theoretical support for the paradigm shift from ‘human-assisted repair’ to ‘AI autonomous repair’.
