AB  - Medical research laboratories increasingly operate heterogeneous computing environments that combine high performance computing (HPC), storage servers, and networked medical devices. Researchers are required to navigate complex IT infrastructure, strict regulations such as HIPAA, GDPR, and the constant threat of data breaches, often without dedicated cybersecurity expertise. Current solutions are manual and fragmented in nature, lacking the integration necessary to ensure a comprehensive, end-to-end security posture. To address these gaps, we developed LabOrchestrator, an AI-driven orchestration framework that unifies automated threat modeling, explainable access control policy synthesis and enforcement, and continuous compliance monitoring into a closed loop lifecycle controller for medical research environments. LabOrchestrator integrates three specialized agents such as ThreatGPT for context-aware threat modeling of lab asset, LLMAC for generating explainable fine grained authorization decisions beyond static RBAC, and ComplianceGPT provides continuous, real-time monitoring of communications and data transfers to proactively prevent HIPAA violations. LabOrchestrator offers a unified orchestration platform that overcomes fragmented and rigid security approaches, enabling a dynamic and adaptive security model. This end-toend framework significantly reduces the compliance burden on researchers, enhances overall security, and facilitates the rapid, secure setup of complex medical environments.
ER  - 

